course: dictionary
lesson: 4235
title: Family words: granddaughter
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A granddaughter is the daughter of your son or daughter. Ruby's mum is Lisa, and Lisa's mum is Nan June. Ruby is June's granddaughter, because Ruby is the daughter of Lisa, who is June's daughter.
explain: In a sentence like «my granddaughter is coming to stay», the words my and granddaughter tell you who the girl is in your family. Grand means one generation further away, so the word always points to two steps: you, then your child, then their child.
explain: Family words often have clues inside them. Grand comes before the word for a child in the family, and great comes before grand to show one more generation. A great-granddaughter is the daughter of your grandchild.
fact: A granddaughter is the daughter of your son or daughter.
fact: «My granddaughter» means the girl who is the daughter of my son or daughter.
fact: «Great-granddaughter» means the daughter of your grandchild, one generation further down.
fact: In a family tree, a granddaughter is two generations below her grandparents.
fact: In stories, grandparents and granddaughters often share adventures together.
exercise: Ruby's mum is Lisa. Lisa's mum is Nan June. Who is Ruby to Nan June? | Great-granddaughter | Cousin | Niece | *Granddaughter
exercise: «My granddaughter is coming to stay this weekend.» Who is coming to stay? | A boy who is my brother | *A girl who is the daughter of my son or daughter | A dog from the next street | My mum's sister
exercise: In a family tree, where does a granddaughter sit compared with her grandparents? | *Two generations below her grandparents | Level with her grandparents, side by side | Above her grandparents | Next to her own parents, as a sister
test: What is a great-granddaughter? | The mother of your father | *The daughter of your grandchild | The girl next door | The sister of your grandmother
test: Which word means the daughter of your son or daughter? | Stepdaughter | Aunt | Niece | *Granddaughter
exam: Which meaning fits «my granddaughter»? | My best friend at school | The son of my sister | My teacher | *The daughter of my son or daughter
